        "parms": "# offer — one-time pairs\noffer stores pairs of ints, an x and a y, and gives each y back once. A y on the right inlet waits for an x, and the next x on the left inlet stores the pair. An x with no y waiting looks its pair up: offer sends the y and deletes the pair. A list <x> <y> stores a pair in one message.\nIt was made for notes that change on the way through a patch. Store each original pitch with the pitch that was played, and when the release arrives, its pitch looks up the one to release. It works as Max's offer does. Nothing is saved with the patch.",
